IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc23-appeals`

-- ccc23-tests-appeals.l4 -- tests for sections 672.72 to 672.78. Expected values are written from the text, never copied from the code.

§ `s 672.72`
-- (1) args: a party; a disposition by a court or Review Board, or a placement decision; to the court of appeal of the province; the ground raises a question of law, fact or mixed law and fact
#ASSERT `s 672.72(1) the party may appeal against the disposition or placement decision` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.72(1) the party may appeal against the disposition or placement decision` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.72(1) the party may appeal against the disposition or placement decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.72(1) the party may appeal against the disposition or placement decision` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.72(1) the party may appeal against the disposition or placement decision` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) args: the day the appellant receives the copy and the reasons (1 March 2026; fifteen days later is 16 March 2026); the day notice is given; a further time directed
#ASSERT `s 672.72(2) notice of appeal is given in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.72(2) notice of appeal is given in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.72(2) notice of appeal is given in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a further time directed by the court of appeal or a judge
#ASSERT `s 672.72(2) notice of appeal is given in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) (JUST (Date 31 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.72(2) notice of appeal is given in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) (JUST (Date 31 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the regulative rule: notice on day 15 -> FULFILLED; the clock passes day 15 -> BREACH
#TRACE `s 672.72(2) the appellant must give notice of appeal within fifteen days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 672.72(2) give notice of appeal` AT 15
#TRACE `s 672.72(2) the appellant must give notice of appeal within fifteen days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 16)
-- (3) args: the day notice is given; the period fixed (days); the day the court of appeal hears the appeal
#ASSERT `s 672.72(3) the court of appeal hears the appeal within the period fixed` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST 30) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.72(3) the court of appeal hears the appeal within the period fixed` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST 30) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no period is fixed in the sources: the text sets no number
#ASSERT `s 672.72(3) the court of appeal hears the appeal within the period fixed` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 672.73 to 672.75`
#ASSERT `s 672.73(1) the appeal is based on a transcript of the proceedings and any other evidence that the court of appeal finds necessary to admit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.73(1) the appeal is based on a transcript of the proceedings and any other evidence that the court of appeal finds necessary to admit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.73(2) subsections 683(1) and (2) apply, with the necessary modifications` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.73(2) subsections 683(1) and (2) apply, with the necessary modifications` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.74(1) the clerk of the court of appeal must notify the court or Review Board that made the disposition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(1) the clerk of the court of appeal must notify the court or Review Board that made the disposition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(2) the court or Review Board must transmit to the court of appeal a copy of the decision, the exhibits and all other material respecting the hearing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(2) the court or Review Board must transmit to the court of appeal a copy of the decision, the exhibits and all other material respecting the hearing` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(3) the clerk of the court of appeal must keep the material with the records of the court of appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(3) the clerk of the court of appeal must keep the material with the records of the court of appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) args: evidence was taken by a stenographer or sound recording apparatus; providing the transcript is contrary to an order or rule
#ASSERT `s 672.74(4) the appellant must provide the court of appeal and the respondent with a certified transcript of the evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(4) the appellant must provide the court of appeal and the respondent with a certified transcript of the evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(4) the appellant must provide the court of appeal and the respondent with a certified transcript of the evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) args: a person other than the appellant failed to comply; that is the only reason for dismissing
#ASSERT `s 672.74(5) the section bars dismissing the appeal by reason only that a person other than the appellant failed to comply` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.74(5) the section bars dismissing the appeal by reason only that a person other than the appellant failed to comply` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.74(5) the section bars dismissing the appeal by reason only that a person other than the appellant failed to comply` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.75 args: a notice of appeal has been filed; the appeal is against a 672.58 disposition
#ASSERT `s 672.75 the application of the disposition is suspended pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.75 the application of the disposition is suspended pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.75 the application of the disposition is suspended pending the determination of the appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 672.76 to 672.8`
#ASSERT `s 672.76(1) the party may apply to a judge of the court of appeal for an order respecting the decision under appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(1) the party may apply to a judge of the court of appeal for an order respecting the decision under appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.76(1) the party may apply to a judge of the court of appeal for an order respecting the decision under appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) args: application made; satisfied that the mental condition justifies it; the order; decision under appeal is a 672.58 disposition; is a 672.54(a) disposition; is a placement decision or 672.54(b)/(c); the disposition is suspended (672.75 or (b)); the placement decision is suspended under (b); the other disposition proposed is under 672.54(a) or 672.58
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(a) direct that a disposition made under section 672.58 be carried out pending the appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(a) direct that a disposition made under section 672.58 be carried out pending the appeal` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(a.1) direct that a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(a) be suspended pending the appeal` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(b) direct that the application of a placement decision or a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or (c) be suspended pending the appeal` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c): where the disposition is suspended, any other disposition, other than under 672.54(a) or 672.58
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(c) make any other disposition pending the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(c) make any other disposition pending the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(c) make any other disposition pending the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d)
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(d) make any other placement decision pending the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(d) make any other placement decision pending the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e) directions to expedite the appeal
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(e) give any directions necessary for expediting the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not satisfied about the mental condition; no application
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE FALSE `s 672.76(2)(e) give any directions necessary for expediting the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.76(2) the judge may make the order pending the determination of the appeal` FALSE TRUE `s 672.76(2)(e) give any directions necessary for expediting the appeal` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(3) the judge must send a copy of the order to each of the parties without delay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.76(3) the judge must send a copy of the order to each of the parties without delay` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 672.77 args: the application of the decision appealed from is suspended; a disposition was in effect before; an interim release or detention order was in effect before; a 672.76(2)(c) disposition has been made
#ASSERT `s 672.77 what is in force pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 672.77 the disposition that was in effect immediately before the decision appealed from took effect`
#ASSERT `s 672.77 what is in force pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 672.77 the order for the interim release or detention of the accused that was in effect immediately before the decision appealed from took effect`
-- "in the absence of a disposition": a disposition takes precedence over the interim order
#ASSERT `s 672.77 what is in force pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 672.77 the disposition that was in effect immediately before the decision appealed from took effect`
-- subject to any disposition made under 672.76(2)(c)
#ASSERT `s 672.77 what is in force pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 672.77 a disposition made under paragraph 672.76(2)(c)`
#ASSERT `s 672.77 what is in force pending the determination of the appeal` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 672.77 not covered`
#ASSERT `s 672.77 what is in force pending the determination of the appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 672.77 not covered`
-- 672.78(1) args: (a) unreasonable or unsupported by the evidence; (b) wrong decision on a question of law; (c) miscarriage of justice
#ASSERT `s 672.78(1) the court of appeal may allow the appeal and set aside the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(1) the court of appeal may allow the appeal and set aside the order` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(1) the court of appeal may allow the appeal and set aside the order` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(1) the court of appeal may allow the appeal and set aside the order` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) args: (a) paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) do not apply; (b) paragraph (1)(b) may apply; no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice
#ASSERT `s 672.78(2) the court of appeal may dismiss the appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(2) the court of appeal may dismiss the appeal` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(2) the court of appeal may dismiss the appeal` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(2) the court of appeal may dismiss the appeal` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(3) the court of appeal may make a disposition or placement decision the Review Board could have made, refer the matter back, or make any other order that justice requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.78(3) the court of appeal may make a disposition or placement decision the Review Board could have made, refer the matter back, or make any other order that justice requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.79 and s 672.8 as the text shows them` EQUALS "672.79 [Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 26] 672.8 [Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 26]"
